      "view": "cv",
      "takeaway": "A user outcome becomes a named requirement and a route-valid scenario. Evidence remains a separate claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "interactions",
      "title": "2 Â· Follow the routed message flow",
      "summary": "Purchase describes the successful exchange order. Arrows below are case after dependencies, not additional software connectors or a measured execution trace.",
      "width": 1080,
      "height": 570,
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "checkout",
          "title": "1 Â· Submit order",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Checkout.submit",
            "browser â†’ application",
            "via checkoutLink"
          ],
          "x": 20,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "The browser requests checkout. Actual endpoints are browser.checkout.submit â†’ application.api.submit on checkoutLink. Delegation reaches application.checkout.api.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.checkout",
          "snippet": "call browser.checkout.submit -> application.api.submit via checkoutLink label checkout;"
        },
        {
          "id": "reserve",
          "title": "2 Â· Reserve stock",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Inventory.reserve",
            "application â†’ inventory",
            "via inventoryLink"
          ],
          "x": 390,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "After checkout, application.inventory.reserve â†’ inventory.api.reserve on inventoryLink. Delegation reaches inventory.stock.api; the request is handled by StockStore.reserve.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.reserve",
          "snippet": "call application.inventory.reserve -> inventory.api.reserve via inventoryLink after checkout label reserve;"
        },
        {
          "id": "stock",
          "title": "3 Â· Return reservation",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Inventory.reserve reply",
            "inventory â†’ application",
            "via inventoryLink"
          ],
          "x": 760,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "After reserve, the correlated Inventory.reserve result travels back through inventoryLink. The successful walkthrough uses quantity 2 against available stock 10.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.stock",
          "snippet": "reply inventory.api.reserve -> application.inventory.reserve via inventoryLink after reserve label stock;"
        },
        {
          "id": "confirmation",
          "title": "4 Â· Publish acceptance",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Checkout.accepted",
            "application â†’ browser",
            "via checkoutLink"
          ],
          "x": 760,
          "y": 350,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "After stock, the case includes application.api.accepted â†’ browser.checkout.accepted through checkoutLink. The event uses the service route in reverse; this row does not claim when the receiving handler completes.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.confirmation",
          "snippet": "publish application.api.accepted -> browser.checkout.accepted via checkoutLink after stock label confirmation;"
        },
        {
          "id": "receipt",
          "title": "5 Â· Publish receipt",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Receipts.created",
            "application â†’ mailer",
            "via receiptLink"
          ],
          "x": 390,
          "y": 350,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "After confirmation, application.receipts.created â†’ mailer.input.created on receiptLink. ReceiptWorker.prepareReceipt owns the receiving handler.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.receipt",
          "snippet": "publish application.receipts.created -> mailer.input.created via receiptLink after confirmation label receipt;"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "title": "6 Â· Return acceptance",
          "kind": "contract",
          "lines": [
            "Checkout.submit reply",
            "application â†’ browser",
            "via checkoutLink"
          ],
          "x": 20,
          "y": 350,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 170,
          "detail": "After receipt, the correlated submit result returns through checkoutLink. BrowserClient.buy then records accepted. Its component lock can delay BrowserClient.confirmation until the request completes.",
          "subject": "WebShop::Purchase.result",
          "snippet": "reply application.api.submit -> browser.checkout.submit via checkoutLink after receipt label result;"
        }
      ],
